WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
The copper tool pushes on the bolt tail. The bolt moves until its stump presses against the rear lever.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.833
The wire lifts the front and middle levers in turn. Each springs back down. The stump is still pressing against the rear lever.

00:00:02.833 --> 00:00:04.667
The wire has to lift the rear lever against both its spring and the stump rubbing on its edge.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:05.250
When the slot in the rear lever reaches the stump, the bolt moves a little. The picker feels that through the copper tool. The stump now sits in the slot and holds the lever as the wire lowers.

